    <p><strong>ProBrothers Construction finishes and remodels basements in <a href="/locations/media/">Media, PA</a> and Delaware County</strong> &mdash; flooring, drywall, lighting, egress windows, and full custom layouts. 15+ years, 5.0 rating, 135+ completed projects. Licensed and insured in Pennsylvania. Free quote within one business day.</p>
  </aside>

  <!-- ===== What Is Basement Finishing ===== -->
  <section class="section svc-overview" id="what-is-basement-finishing" aria-label="What Is Basement Finishing">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="svc-overview__grid">
        <div class="svc-overview__content reveal" data-reveal="left">
          <span class="section__kicker">SERVICE OVERVIEW</span>
          <h2 class="section__title">
            Basement Finishing in Media, PA
            <svg class="blueprint" viewBox="0 0 160 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M0,12 C40,4 80,20 120,10 L160,14" stroke-width="2.5" style="--len:220"/>
              <circle cx="8" cy="12" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
              <circle cx="152" cy="13" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
            </svg>
          </h2>
          <p class="svc-overview__para">Basement finishing converts an unfinished or underutilized basement into a livable, functional space — home office, recreation room, gym, guest suite, wet bar, or playroom. In Delaware County, PA, basement finishing and remodeling typically costs between <strong>$15,000 and $45,000</strong> depending on square footage, complexity, and finishes. ProBrothers has completed basement projects across <a href="/locations/media/">Media</a>, <a href="/locations/glen-mills/">Glen Mills</a>, Newtown Square, and Delaware County since 2009.</p>
          <p class="svc-overview__para">Our team manages every step — framing, electrical, HVAC rough-in, drywall, flooring, and trim. We pull all required permits in Media, PA and surrounding municipalities and handle inspections through to the certificate of occupancy. Projects with a full bathroom addition or wet bar are part of our broader <a href="/services/additions/">home additions</a> scope as well.</p>
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn--accent btn--lg" data-magnetic>Request a Free Quote</a>
        </div>
        <div class="svc-overview__media reveal" data-reveal="right">
          <figure class="svc-overview__figure">
            <img src="/assets/img/services/fireplace.webp"
                 alt="Custom fireplace and entertainment built-ins in a finished basement by ProBrothers"
                 loading="lazy" width="768" height="1024" />
            <figcaption>Finished Basement, Media PA</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="svc-overview__figure">
            <img src="/assets/img/services/fireplace-1.webp"
                 alt="Elegant basement entertainment space built by ProBrothers in Delaware County"
                 loading="lazy" width="768" height="1024" />
            <figcaption>Delaware County Project</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== Basement Finishing: Unfinished to Livable ===== -->
  <section class="section svc-why-trim" id="unfinished-to-livable" aria-label="Basement Finishing: Unfinished to Livable" style="background:var(--gray-2)">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head reveal">
        <span class="section__kicker">FULL FINISH</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">
          UNFINISHED BASEMENT TO LIVABLE SPACE
          <svg class="blueprint" viewBox="0 0 160 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M0,12 C40,4 80,20 120,10 L160,14" stroke-width="2.5" style="--len:220"/>
            <circle cx="8" cy="12" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
            <circle cx="152" cy="13" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
          </svg>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-why-trim__grid">
        <div class="svc-why-trim__text reveal">
          <p>The most common scope is a full finish of an unfinished basement: insulation between studs, moisture barrier, drywall, drop ceiling or drywall ceiling, LVP or engineered hardwood flooring, recessed lighting, and at least one egress window for code compliance. ProBrothers manages every step — framing, electrical, HVAC rough-in, drywall, flooring, and trim.</p>
          <p>A standard basement finish in Delaware County (700&ndash;1,000 sq ft) typically runs <strong>$15,000&ndash;$25,000</strong>. Projects with a full bathroom addition, wet bar, or multiple defined rooms run $25,000&ndash;$45,000. We pull all required permits in <a href="/locations/media/">Media, PA</a> and surrounding municipalities and handle inspections through to the certificate of occupancy.</p>
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn--accent btn--lg" style="margin-top:1rem;display:inline-block" data-magnetic>Get a Free Basement Finish Quote</a>
        </div>
        <blockquote class="svc-testimonial reveal" data-reveal="right">
          <div class="review__stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>
          <p>&ldquo;We hired them for a full basement remodel. What stood out most was their communication. We received daily updates on what was happening, and there were no surprise costs at the end. The finished entertainment space is exactly what we envisioned.&rdquo;</p>
          <footer>Jessica T., Media, PA</footer>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== Home Office, Gym & Rec Rooms ===== -->
  <section class="section" id="home-office-gym-rec" aria-label="Home Office, Gym & Recreation Rooms">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head reveal">
        <span class="section__kicker">PURPOSE-BUILT SPACES</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">
          HOME OFFICE, GYM &amp; RECREATION ROOMS
          <svg class="blueprint" viewBox="0 0 160 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M0,12 C40,4 80,20 120,10 L160,14" stroke-width="2.5" style="--len:220"/>
            <circle cx="8" cy="12" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
            <circle cx="152" cy="13" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
          </svg>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-prose reveal">
        <p>Finished basements in Delaware County homes are increasingly used for home offices, home gyms, and family recreation rooms. ProBrothers designs and builds purpose-specific layouts: soundproofed home office spaces with built-in shelving, gym rooms with rubber flooring and wall mirrors, and rec rooms with LVP flooring, feature walls, and built-in media cabinetry.</p>
        <p>We can divide a large open basement into multiple defined rooms using framed partition walls, each with independent lighting circuits &mdash; giving you a home office, a gym, and a storage room all from the same footprint. This work complements our full <a href="/services/remodeling/">home remodeling</a> scope for homeowners undertaking multi-room renovations.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== Wet Bar & Entertainment Spaces ===== -->
  <section class="section" id="wet-bar-entertainment" aria-label="Wet Bar & Entertainment Spaces" style="background:var(--gray-2)">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head reveal">
        <span class="section__kicker">ENTERTAINMENT</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">
          WET BAR &amp; ENTERTAINMENT SPACES
          <svg class="blueprint" viewBox="0 0 160 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M0,12 C40,4 80,20 120,10 L160,14" stroke-width="2.5" style="--len:220"/>
            <circle cx="8" cy="12" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
            <circle cx="152" cy="13" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
          </svg>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-prose reveal">
        <p>A basement wet bar is one of the highest-ROI additions in a Delaware County home remodel. ProBrothers builds custom wet bars with granite or quartz countertops, custom cabinetry, under-counter refrigerators, sink plumbing, and tile backsplash. We also install dedicated electrical circuits for bar appliances and under-cabinet LED lighting.</p>
        <p>For entertainment-focused basements, we build home theater rooms with acoustic ceiling and wall treatments, in-ceiling speaker rough-in, and large-format tile or LVP flooring. Media room setups in Delaware County typically add $5,000&ndash;$15,000 to a base basement finish project. Our <a href="/services/cabinets/">custom cabinetry</a> team handles all built-in storage and media cabinetry.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== Egress Windows & Permits ===== -->
  <section class="section" id="egress-windows-permits" aria-label="Egress Windows & Permits">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head reveal">
        <span class="section__kicker">CODE &amp; SAFETY</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">
          EGRESS WINDOWS &amp; PERMITS
          <svg class="blueprint" viewBox="0 0 160 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M0,12 C40,4 80,20 120,10 L160,14" stroke-width="2.5" style="--len:220"/>
            <circle cx="8" cy="12" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
            <circle cx="152" cy="13" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
          </svg>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-prose reveal">
        <p>Pennsylvania code requires at least one egress window in any finished basement that includes a sleeping room (bedroom). Even for non-bedroom finished basements, egress windows are strongly recommended for fire safety and required for full certificate of occupancy in most Delaware County municipalities.</p>
        <p>ProBrothers installs egress window wells — cutting the foundation wall, installing a steel well, and framing the window opening. Egress window installation in Delaware County typically costs <strong>$2,500&ndash;$4,500 per window</strong> including excavation and waterproofing. We handle the permit application and the inspection through to sign-off.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

