  <!-- ===== FAQ ===== -->
  <section class="section svc-faq" id="faq" aria-label="Frequently Asked Questions">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head reveal">
        <span class="section__kicker">HAVE QUESTIONS?</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">
          FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS
          <svg class="blueprint" viewBox="0 0 160 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M0,12 C40,4 80,20 120,10 L160,14" stroke-width="2.5" style="--len:220"/>
            <circle cx="8" cy="12" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
            <circle cx="152" cy="13" r="3" style="--len:20"/>
          </svg>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item reveal">
          <dt class="faq-item__q">
            <button aria-expanded="false" class="faq-item__btn">
              How much does it cost to finish a basement in Delaware County, PA?
              <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            </button>
          </dt>
          <dd class="faq-item__a">
            <p>Basement finishing in Delaware County, PA typically costs between <strong>$15,000 and $45,000</strong>. A basic finish &mdash; framing, drywall, flooring, and lighting &mdash; for a 700&ndash;1,000 sq ft basement runs $15,000&ndash;$25,000. A full basement remodel with a wet bar, bathroom rough-in, or multiple defined rooms runs $25,000&ndash;$45,000. Projects with egress windows, a home theater room, or premium finishes push toward the upper range. ProBrothers provides a free, itemized quote within one business day.</p>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal" style="--d:.07s">
          <dt class="faq-item__q">
            <button aria-expanded="false" class="faq-item__btn">
              How long does a basement finish take in Media, PA?
              <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            </button>
          </dt>
          <dd class="faq-item__a">
            <p>Most basement finishing projects in Media, PA take <strong>6 to 10 weeks</strong> from permit issuance to final inspection. A straightforward open-plan finish takes 6&ndash;8 weeks. A complex project with a bathroom, wet bar, and multiple rooms takes 8&ndash;12 weeks. Permit approval in Delaware County typically takes 2&ndash;3 weeks &mdash; we submit the application before work begins to minimize delays. ProBrothers provides a written schedule before the project starts.</p>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal" style="--d:.14s">
          <dt class="faq-item__q">
            <button aria-expanded="false" class="faq-item__btn">
              Do I need a permit to finish a basement in Delaware County, PA?
              <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            </button>
