          <dd class="faq-item__a">
            <p>Yes. Basement finishing in Delaware County requires a building permit because it involves electrical work, possibly plumbing, and a change of use from unfinished to livable space. Without a permit, the work is unpermitted and can create problems when selling the home. ProBrothers handles all permit applications and inspections in <a href="/locations/media/">Media</a>, Springfield, Newtown Square, <a href="/locations/glen-mills/">Glen Mills</a>, and surrounding municipalities.</p>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal" style="--d:.21s">
